From 8c219e49437176475c055bafbed6a6f271ce8276 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:22:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 77/78] PlaitOS: plait_backup and icon pack review fixes

plait_backup:
- Restores hold the package manager's freezer (new
  PackageManagerInternal.plaitFreezePackage) for the whole data
  replacement, instead of a one-off force-stop: nothing can start the
  app on half-restored data.
- Never restore into privileged apps or system apps as shipped (data,
  permissions, or an APK update over them); backing them up is fine.
- Android/data, obb and media are on primary (internal) storage, not on
  the app's volume.
- The broker manager, its key, grant checks and the audit log are the
  caller's own user's.
- Uid-mode app-ops (All files access, exact alarms, ...) are backed up
  as "Uid mode: OP: mode" lines and restored with setUidMode, under the
  same rule as package modes.
- APK installs: the archive must end with the end-of-archive block, the
  rest of the stream is drained, and the unpacking must have finished
  without errors before the session is committed.

Icon packs:
- The pack is reloaded when it was updated, or retried after a failed
  load, checked at most once a minute (long-lived processes kept stale
  icons until they restarted).
- HashMap instead of ArrayMap (large appfilters took quadratic time),
  and the parser or asset stream is closed.
- An activity with its own icon no longer gets the pack's icon for the
  app; only activities showing the app's icon do.

